1
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:10,660
T minus 60 seconds

2
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:13,030
Oh, it all comes down to this!

3
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:14,720
Oh, I've got butterflies.

4
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,510
Don't get soft on me, Hofstadter.

5
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:19,510
I will slap those glasses right off your face.

6
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,340
What's going on?

7
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:25,070
Hey. We're about to buy tickets for Comic-Con.

8
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,390
T Minus 45 seconds!

9
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:29,750
They sell out incredibly fast,

10
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,990
but as long as one of us gets in, we can buy passes...

11
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:32,240
Good Lord, this is not the time for flirting!

12
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,300
Keep it in your pants!

13
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:38,470
It's a whole lot of weird before coffee.

14
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:40,390
T-minus 30 seconds!

15
00:00:40,390 --> 00:00:42,760
Oh, I have to go to the bathroom so bad.

16
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,030
Every year! I told you, wear a diaper!

17
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,770
And I told you I get diaper rash!

18
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:48,040
15 seconds!

19
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,140
Oh, this is it!

20
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,290
This is it!

21
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,170
This is it.

22
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:58,020
Five, four, three,

23
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:59,760
- two, one. - It's live.

24
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,200
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

25
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:09,020
Anyone in?!

26
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,070
- No! - Not yet!

27
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:13,790
Do not stop refreshing your screens!

28
00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:15,290
- Refresh. - Refresh.

29
00:01:15,290 --> 00:01:16,260
Refresh.

30
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,370
Refresh. Refresh.

31
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:20,520
Refresh. Refresh. Refresh...

32
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:23,190
Yeah, this is not gonna be enough coffee.

33
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:25,180
Refresh. Refresh. Refresh.

34
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:54,600
Refresh... Refresh... Refresh...

35
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,370
Refresh... Refresh...

36
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:58,500
Refresh. Refresh.

37
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,870
Refresh.

38
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,500
Refresh. It's been ten minutes!

39
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,830
We're running out of time.

40
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,310
To be cool? Yeah.

41
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:07,650
I did it! I did it! I'm in the queue!

42
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:13,070
And they say firefighters are the real heroes.

43
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,300
Uh, what number in line are you?

44
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,590
- Uh, 15... - Great!

45
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,590
- ...thousand, 211. - Damn!

46
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,920
Oh, they only have Thursday and Sunday passes left.

47
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:25,090
- Really? - Oh, Thursday's gone. Just Sunday left.

48
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:28,450
Oh, Sunday's the worst. Everybody's leaving,

49
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,150
most of good panels are over,

50
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:34,720
the only T-shirts left are small and XXXXL

51
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:37,360
Sunday's gone.

52
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,800
Not Sunday! I love Sunday!

53
00:02:42,190 --> 00:02:45,160
So that's it? Everything's sold out?

54
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,940
Yeah.

55
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:50,430
I can't believe we're not going.

56
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:52,410
It's okay.

57
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:56,740
You know, there-there's always WonderCon in Anaheim.

58
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,930
That-That's just as good.

59
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,520
Excuse me.

60
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,570
Oh, guys, this is really sad.

61
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:15,280
And in a different way than it was 20 minutes ago.

62
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:20,870
I can't believe we wasted all that time on our Hulk costumes.

63
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:22,700
You were all going as the Hulk?

64
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,270
Not the same Hulk.

65
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:27,340
Ferrigno, Bana, Norton and Ruffalo.

66
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:30,650
We would have been the angry green belles

67
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:33,000
of the masquerade ball.

68
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,540
Yeah.

69
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:39,910
And we're back to the first kind of sad.

70
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:46,570
Gentlemen, I have the solution to our Comic-Con problem.

71
00:03:46,570 --> 00:03:48,330
We don't need them.

72
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,780
I'm starting my own convention.

73
00:03:52,610 --> 00:03:55,210
Sheldon, just buy scalped tickets with us.

74
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:58,790
I told you. Buying scalped tickets is against the rules.

75
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:02,320
If you get caught, you get banned from Comic-Con for life.

76
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,750
Life, Leonard.

77
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:06,080
You're gonna feel pretty silly when we're 80 years old,

78
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:08,020
and you have to drive me down there

79
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:10,160
and then wait in the car for three days.

80
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,140
Do what you want.

81
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:13,650
We're getting scalped tickets.

82
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:15,890
Oh, I already found a guy online who's willing to sell.

83
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:18,400
How do you know this isn't a sting operation

84
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:21,380
set up by the Comic-Con police?

85
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:22,460
The same way I know

86
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:25,630
that the people in the TV set can't see me.

87
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,530
Sheldon, just come with us.

88
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:29,730
You're not gonna make your own convention.

89
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:30,940
You know, there was a time

90
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,000
when Comic-Con didn't exist at all

91
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,720
until one lone dreamer with a unique vision made it happen.

92
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:38,130
And you mark my words--

93
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:40,620
I'm gonna rip that guy off.

94
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:46,730
Yes, I'm starting my own comic book convention,

95
00:04:46,730 --> 00:04:49,760
and I thought that your client, Robert Downey Jr.,

96
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:54,010
would be perfect to appear on our first panel.

97
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:56,090
Oh, well, now, why are you saying "no"?

98
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:58,370
You haven't even asked him yet.

99
00:04:58,740 --> 00:04:59,610
You know, excuse me,

100
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:01,270
but I sat through Iron Man 2.

101
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:04,310
I believe he owes me two hours of his time.

102
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:08,070
They hung up on me.

103
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,490
Did you tell them that you're holding your convention

104
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:14,580
at a Marie Callender's,

105
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:17,810
and that every panelist gets a free slice of pie?

106
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:20,650
I didn't even get to that part.

107
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,520
Look, even your friend Wil Wheaton thinks

108
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,020
this is a waste of time.

109
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,570
Not true.

110
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:27,430
Wil thinks this is a great idea.

111
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,050
He was just concerned that

112
00:05:29,050 --> 00:05:30,500
he wasn't a big enough celebrity

113
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,630
to headline such an amazing event.

114
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:36,440
Also, that's the same day that he shampoos his beard.

115
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:38,650
Sheldon, buddy, I just don't think

116
00:05:38,650 --> 00:05:40,410
this is going to come together for you.

117
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:42,010
You don't know that.

118
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:44,920
I still have plenty of solid leads on this list.

119
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,430
- Good luck. - No, wait.

120
00:05:46,430 --> 00:05:49,170
I need you to call Stan Lee, Leonard Nimoy

121
00:05:49,170 --> 00:05:51,710
and Bill Nye the Science Guy...

122
00:05:51,710 --> 00:05:54,680
'cause, legally, I'm not allowed to.

123
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,920
Oh, and, also, Carrie Fisher,

124
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:59,430
you know, 'cause I hear she can be pretty nuts.

125
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,960
I can't believe Leonard is

126
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,300
spending hundreds of dollars on scalped tickets.

127
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:08,310
Last week, you spent that on a little dress.

128
00:06:08,310 --> 00:06:10,620
Yeah, but those tickets only get him into Comic-Con.

129
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,690
That dress gets me into anywhere I want.

130
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:17,260
Those tickets were pretty expensive.

131
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:20,740
I had to give Howie an advance on his allowance.

132
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,850
Now he's never gonna put his toys away.

133
00:06:25,490 --> 00:06:27,330
Why can't they do something sensible like Sheldon

134
00:06:27,330 --> 00:06:30,070
and start their own comic book convention?

135
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:34,060
Also, who wants to throw me out that window?

136
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:37,000
Oh, while they're acting like teenagers,

137
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,510
we could do something grown-up.

138
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,300
Oh. You mean like a museum?

139
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:44,160
Yes, like a museum, but anything else.

140
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,870
Oh, I know. There's a nice hotel not far from here

141
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:49,590
where they do afternoon tea.

142
00:06:49,590 --> 00:06:52,300
Ooh, afternoon tea-- how sophisticated of us.

143
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,800
Oh, all right, if we're gonna be fancy,

144
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,440
I should probably put on clean underwear.

145
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:57,800
La-dee-da!

146
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,260
Look who has clean underwear.

147
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:01,330
No, we're gonna stop at Target on the way.

148
00:07:04,690 --> 00:07:06,370
Hey, since Sheldon's not going to Comic-Con,

149
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:09,070
maybe we could find a cool trio to dress up as.

150
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:11,400
What if we go as The Fantastic Four,

151
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:12,850
and just tell people that the Invisible Girl

152
00:07:12,850 --> 00:07:14,810
is standing there with us.

153
00:07:15,590 --> 00:07:17,130
Oh, and I thought our days of pretending

154
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:19,590
to be with women who don't exist were over.

155
00:07:20,530 --> 00:07:23,230
Gentlemen, I am one step away

156
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:26,450
from securing a huge guest for my convention.

157
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:28,190
Does that step include chloroform

158
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:30,370
and a roll of duct tape?

159
00:07:30,370 --> 00:07:31,920
I don't think that will be necessary

160
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,130
for Mr. James Earl Jones.

161
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,190
You heard me.

162
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:36,620
The voice of Darth Vader,

163
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:38,260
the Lion King's dad,

164
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:43,610
and FYI, the guy who says, "This is CNN."

165
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:46,240
Which also sounds like Darth Vader.

166
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:50,690
How are you gonna get James Earl Jones?

167
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:53,280
Simple. Earlier today, he Tweeted

168
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,330
that he's looking forward to going to

169
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:56,860
his favorite sushi restaurant for dinner.

170
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:59,620
I Googled an interview from four years ago

171
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:02,690
which was conducted in his favorite sushi restaurant.

172
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:05,850
That's where he'll be, and that's where I'm going,

173
00:08:05,850 --> 00:08:07,620
- and... - And that's where Darth Vader's

174
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,870
gonna pour soy sauce on your head.

175
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,940
Sheldon, I don't care if you get scalped tickets with us or not,

176
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:16,990
but please don't be creepy and go stalking this poor guy.

177
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:18,700
You're gonna get in trouble.

178
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,880
You're the ones who are going to get in trouble.

179
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,030
You're buying non-transferable tickets.

180
00:08:23,030 --> 00:08:25,250
And from a stranger, no less.

181
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:27,360
Not only can you get banned from Comic-Con,

182
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:30,200
if caught, you could be charged with petty theft.

183
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:33,000
You think about that while I'm warning James Earl Jones

184
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,660
about the danger of posting his location on Twitter.

185
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:38,170
He got lucky this time.

186
00:08:38,170 --> 00:08:40,940
There are some weirdoes out there.

187
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,260
Forgot my keys.

188
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:04,730
Okay, great. Bye.

189
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:06,620
Our friendly neighborhood scalper

190
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,310
says he's running late.

191
00:09:08,310 --> 00:09:10,560
Does he sound like a criminal?

192
00:09:11,930 --> 00:09:13,140
What do you mean?

193
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,430
You know, did he say things like,

194
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:19,370
"Youse guys," or "listen here, see?"

195
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:22,620
Yes. He-He's late

196
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:25,910
because he's on his way here from 1940.

197
00:09:27,010 --> 00:09:27,670
I'm just saying.

198
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:28,880
We don't know who this guy is.

199
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:31,020
What if he wants to steal our money or our kidneys,

200
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:33,970
or make a suit out of our skins?

201
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:37,470
Why would someone want to make clothes out of your skin?

202
00:09:37,470 --> 00:09:38,310
I don't know.

203
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:41,600
Maybe 'cause dark doesn't show the stains?

204
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:43,970
Well, now you're making me wonder

205
00:09:43,970 --> 00:09:46,240
if we should have met him at a neutral location.

206
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:49,270
Why do you think I told him to come to your place?

207
00:09:58,090 --> 00:09:59,960
There sure are a lot of little kids here.

208
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,100
I can't believe we thought this would makes us feel grown up.

209
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:05,240
I can't believe the waiter thought I was your daughter.

210
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,130
Well, last time I got dressed up

211
00:10:09,130 --> 00:10:11,110
and had tea was when I was five.

212
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:13,990
Just me, my teddy bear, Raggedy Ann and my hamster.

213
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:16,060
- That's cute. - It was.

214
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:19,050
Till my hamster ate all her babies.

215
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:24,200
It got less cute really fast.

216
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:25,880
Should we leave?

217
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,380
Well, there's a bar in the lobby.

218
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,310
I could go for a drink.

219
00:10:29,610 --> 00:10:32,240
Drinking in the afternoon, just like her mommy.

220
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:47,430
Let me guess.

221
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:51,900
You like Star Wars.

222
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:56,850
You know, I've been in other movies.

223
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,940
But you don't care about those, do you?

224
00:11:09,290 --> 00:11:12,840
I have one thing to say to people like you...

225
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,390
I like Star Wars too.

226
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:20,300
Care to join me?

227
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,310
Thank you.

228
00:11:23,810 --> 00:11:24,910
My friend Leonard said

229
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:26,450
if I bothered you while you were eating,

230
00:11:26,450 --> 00:11:28,590
you'd think I was a creepy stalker.

231
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:34,230
Well your friend Leonard sounds like a real weenie.

232
00:11:36,450 --> 00:11:40,370
He is, Mr. Earl Jones, he is.

233
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:45,350
Okay, so, I'm on a Comic-Con message board,

234
00:11:45,350 --> 00:11:47,490
and there's a post from a guy

235
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,730
where he says he got caught using someone else's badge...

236
00:11:50,730 --> 00:11:51,870
and Sheldon was right--

237
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:54,750
he did get charged with petty theft. Guys...

238
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,670
if I go to jail dressed as the Human Torch,

239
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,380
that might send the wrong message.

240
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,920
Maybe this isn't a good idea.

241
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:08,160
I can text the guy and tell him we changed our minds.

242
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:10,890
Do it.

243
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:12,220
Okay.

244
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:15,750
We're officially not going to Comic-Con.

245
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:19,650
Hold on. We always do this.

246
00:12:19,650 --> 00:12:21,500
- Do what? - Chicken out.

247
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,550
We're-we're so afraid of getting into trouble

248
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:25,530
that we never do anything wrong.

249
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:26,820
That's 'cause we're the good guys.

250
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:28,820
Even Batman breaks the rules.

251
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:31,410
You know I struggle with Batman.

252
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:34,670
I-I say, this one time,

253
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:37,960
instead of wimping out, let's be badasses!

254
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,260
Okay, I'll be a badass--

255
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:43,090
but only if you pinky-swear to be one, too.

256
00:12:44,990 --> 00:12:47,160
- Howard, you in on this? - No need.

257
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,720
I'm breaking rules all the time.

258
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:52,840
- Name one. - Last night.

259
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:56,660
Drank my Pepto straight out of the bottle.

260
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:59,780
What about that little cup they give you?

261
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:01,210
Yeah.

262
00:13:02,070 --> 00:13:04,070
What about it?

263
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:08,310
A-Are you impressed by that?

264
00:13:08,310 --> 00:13:10,890
- A little. - Yeah, me, too.

265
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:16,960
You know, when I first read the script for Empire Strikes Back

266
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:20,440
and Darth Vader told Luke he was his father...

267
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,900
...I thought for sure he was lying.

268
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:24,870
Me, too!

269
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:26,320
But he wasn't, was he?

270
00:13:26,370 --> 00:13:28,070
He was not!

271
00:13:28,070 --> 00:13:30,790
How messed up was that?!

272
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,520
So messed up.

273
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:36,530
What do you say let's go have some fun?

274
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:37,610
My wife's in New York,

275
00:13:37,610 --> 00:13:39,740
and I got a Lion King residual check

276
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:42,390
burning a hole in my pocket.

277
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:47,150
So, afternoon tea was a bust.

278
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,810
On the bright side, every six-year-old there

279
00:13:48,810 --> 00:13:51,450
was jealous of my tiara.

280
00:13:52,450 --> 00:13:55,600
Not gonna lie-- it felt good.

281
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:57,840
Let me ask you a question:

282
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,500
When did you guys start feeling grown up?

283
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,610
'Cause I am not sure I do.

284
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:03,820
Honestly, I thought when I got married I would,

285
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:06,570
but I still kind of feel like I'm pretending.

286
00:14:06,570 --> 00:14:10,610
It doesn't help that most of my clothes come from Gap Kids.

287
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,940
Okay, so I'm an adult,

288
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:15,720
and the other day I saw an old man slip and fall down,

289
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:18,060
and I laughed.

290
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:20,740
I mean, I laughed hard.

291
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,480
Like-like, out loud.

292
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:26,040
If he was conscious, he would've heard me.

293
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:27,930
- Oh, my gosh. - I know.

294
00:14:27,930 --> 00:14:29,760
One of the tennis balls came off his walker

295
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:32,400
and bounced right off his head. I mean...

296
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:37,590
I... I almost wet myself.

297
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:39,900
I guess you had to be there.

298
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,350
I think I have you both beat.

299
00:14:42,350 --> 00:14:43,470
Imagine trying to feel like a grown-up

300
00:14:43,470 --> 00:14:45,310
when you've never even been with a man.

301
00:14:45,310 --> 00:14:47,730
Okay, sex is not what makes you a grown-up.

302
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:51,180
Yeah. Or you'd be the oldest one here.

303
00:14:52,570 --> 00:14:53,610
Really?

304
00:14:53,610 --> 00:14:56,360
Is that how you talk to your mother?

305
00:15:00,110 --> 00:15:01,550
He just parked. He's on his way up.

306
00:15:01,550 --> 00:15:02,820
Good. This is exciting.

307
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:04,640
- It is. I feel alive. - Yeah.

308
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,790
What if we do get caught; who cares?

309
00:15:06,790 --> 00:15:08,400
So we get banned from Comic-Con.

310
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:10,270
- Maybe slapped with a fine. - Oh, no.

311
00:15:10,270 --> 00:15:12,170
I'll be an astronaut and a bad boy--

312
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:15,090
how will women keep their pants on?

313
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:18,370
Uh, maybe it'll come up when I apply for citizenship.

314
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:23,100
Oh, crap, what if it comes up when I apply for citizenship?

315
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:25,030
I wonder if we'd have to disclose something like this

316
00:15:25,030 --> 00:15:27,440
when we apply for grants.

317
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,060
He's gonna be here any second-- what should we do?

318
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,350
You guys are such babies.

319
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:33,270
I'll handle this.

320
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,900
If he thinks we're not home, he'll go away.

321
00:15:38,990 --> 00:15:39,910
I thought you were a badass.

322
00:15:39,910 --> 00:15:43,160
I lied about the Pepto-- I always use the little cup!

323
00:15:49,530 --> 00:15:53,130
Is it true, as a child, you were a stutterer

324
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:56,320
and were functionally mute for eight years?

325
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,950
It is true.

326
00:15:57,950 --> 00:16:01,640
Is it true they used scuba gear

327
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:04,010
to create the sound of Darth Vader breathing?

328
00:16:04,010 --> 00:16:05,960
They sure did.

329
00:16:06,990 --> 00:16:10,800
Is it true that you were premed in college

330
00:16:10,830 --> 00:16:12,510
and you almost became a doctor?

331
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,730
That's right.

332
00:16:13,730 --> 00:16:16,010
Oh, James!

333
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:19,350
I could listen to your stories all night.

334
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:30,870
I mean, really, what's so great about being grown up?

335
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:35,400
Well, for starters, we'd be splitting this check three ways.

336
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:38,570
I'm serious. Who wants to do all that stuff?

337
00:16:38,570 --> 00:16:40,580
Have insurance, pay mortgages,

338
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:44,300
leave one of those little notes when you hit a parked car.

339
00:16:44,850 --> 00:16:47,470
I told you it was Penny.

340
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,090
Oh, come on, it wasn't me.

341
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:50,770
Anyone could have knocked your mirror off...

342
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:53,320
or whatever happened.

343
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:57,210
Maybe the guys are right.

344
00:16:57,210 --> 00:16:59,390
I mean, we spent the whole night trying to be mature,

345
00:16:59,390 --> 00:17:00,960
and it was kind of boring.

346
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:03,560
I'm sure they're having more fun than we are.

347
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:06,590
Oh, God, I could really use

348
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:09,310
exactly two tablespoons of Pepto right now.

349
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,780
Hey, Los Angeles!

350
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:25,480
I'm on a Ferris wheel with Darth Vader!

351
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,840
And he's nicer than you think!

352
00:17:29,390 --> 00:17:31,640
I am!

353
00:17:35,110 --> 00:17:38,740
* In the jungle, the mighty jungle *

354
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,730
* The lion sleeps tonight *

355
00:17:41,730 --> 00:17:44,540
Bring it home, Mufasa.

356
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:54,020
I don't understand what we're doing.

357
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:57,380
Whose house is that?

358
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:59,360
Carrie Fisher.

359
00:17:59,670 --> 00:18:00,950
And she's a little crazy,

360
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:03,550
so get ready to run.

361
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:20,620
It's not funny anymore, James!

362
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:24,040
Then why am I laughing!

363
00:18:32,330 --> 00:18:34,380
Ah, Sheldon, this is the perfect end

364
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,720
to a perfect night.

365
00:18:37,930 --> 00:18:39,750
Okay.

366
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:44,320
Yeah, but I think it could have ended with the karaoke.

367
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:47,690
What were you trying to ask me at the strip club?

368
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:53,710
How much does it cost to get them off my lap?

369
00:18:53,710 --> 00:18:56,160
No. Something about a convention.

370
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:58,470
Oh, right! Well...

371
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:01,410
my friends and I couldn't get into Comic-Con this year,

372
00:19:01,410 --> 00:19:04,290
and I was trying to start my own convention,

373
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:06,360
and I was going to ask

374
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,890
if you would be a panelist.

375
00:19:08,890 --> 00:19:11,580
Why don't you and your friends come to Comic-Con with me?

376
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:13,190
- Really? - Of course.

377
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:15,460
And San Diego is right across the border

378
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,830
from my favorite city on Earth,

379
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:20,800
Tijuana...

380
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:24,580
...where I'm taking you every night!

381
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:28,730
Ay-yi-yi.

382
00:19:28,730 --> 00:19:32,380
Ay-yi-yi, bang-bang.

383
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:40,520
So, Beau Bridges is on my shoulders,

384
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:44,240
and Jeff Bridges is on Marlon Brando's shoulders,

385
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,810
and remember, we do not have permission to be in the pool--

386
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:50,310
Hey! Sheldon, wake up!

387
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:50,930
And...

388
00:19:50,930 --> 00:19:53,750
Angie Dickinson is about to sic the dogs on us,

389
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:56,430
and I go under the water and Marlon goes under the water,

390
00:19:56,430 --> 00:19:58,330
and the water raises about two feet

391
00:19:58,330 --> 00:19:59,760
and sloshes all over her patio,

392
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,740
and the dogs freak out and run like hell,

393
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:03,100
and then we run like hell...

394
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,370
Oh, boy!

395
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:08,190
That was a lot of fun.

396
00:20:09,430 --> 00:20:12,630
Uh... who's Angie Dickinson?

